{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"## RCA (Phase 1 complete) — confirmed root cause\n\n**Mechanism (runtime-confirmed).** In `PydanticAIRunner.run()` (src/rebar/llm/runner.py) the\nfinalization tail runs `log_call_success(...)` → `result = _findings.finalize_outcome(...)` →\n`_merge_success_run_shape(...)` → `record_call_spend(...)`, all AFTER the ProviderSession\n`with` and the agent-call `try/except/finally` have exited. `record_call_spend` is the last\nstatement. When `finalize_outcome` raises (e.g. schema validation on a structured/\nverify_completion call whose model call already succeeded and burned tokens), the exception\npropagates straight out of `run()` before `record_call_spend` executes, so no spend row is\nwritten to usage.jsonl / the billable sink. `log_call_success` (emitted before finalize) does\nfire, so the loss is silent — cost reporting undercounts real token spend.\n\n**Proof (discriminating experiment).** The c465 characterization test monkeypatches\n`finalize_outcome` to raise and `record_call_spend` to capture calls, drives `run()`, and\nobserves: the \"llm call ... ok in\" success log DID fire, and `spend_calls == []` — i.e.\nrecord_call_spend never ran. Rewriting that assertion to demand exactly one spend row makes the\ntest RED against current code (`assert 0 == 1`) for exactly this reason, GREEN after the fix.\n\n**Legitimacy = defect.** Authority: bug 8455 established the invariant \"a call that burned\ntokens must leave a spend row even on the failure path\" (fixed for the agent-call except\nboundary); `record_call_spend`'s own docstring (\"Durable spend record for the weekly billable\nCI jobs\"); and this ticket's acceptance criteria. This finalize boundary is the mirror gap\n8455's fix did not reach.\n\n**Attribution (`caused_by` = 8455-a818-f305-4748), class = preexisting (omission).** The\nordering (spend recorded after finalize, unguarded) predates the ADR-0056 extraction: commit\n`8b44b5aa50ee` (ticket 5e75) moved the inline `usage_log.record` spend line into\n`record_call_spend` as an explicit \"Pure relocation: no behaviour change\", preserving the\nposition. There is no commit that *broke* previously-working behavior — the finalize-raise path\nnever recorded spend — so this is an omission, not a regression. It is attributed by\nscope-of-work to bug **8455** (`8455-a818-f305-4748`, commits c179971eab2d / fc3fc19787a6,\n\"record usage for a failed LLM call\"): 8455 is the ticket that introduced the failure-path\nspend contract and whose scope should have covered this mirror boundary. Recorded as\n`preexisting` because the gap existed independently of and prior to 8455's partial fix.\n\n**Fix.** Wrap `finalize_outcome` in `try/except Exception: record_call_spend(...); raise`. This\nrecords the spend row for the already-consumed tokens on the finalize-failure path and re-raises\nthe original exception unchanged (disposition preserved — the caller still sees the ValueError).\nThe failure-path row carries the authoritative token counts (known before finalize); it omits\nthe success-only `_merge_success_run_shape` enrichment (which needs the finalized result),\nexactly mirroring 8455's agent-call except-path row. The SUCCESS path is byte-identical:\n`record_call_spend` still runs last, after the shape merge, so the success spend row is\nunchanged. Options (b) \"move record_call_spend before finalize\" and try/finally were rejected\nbecause both reorder the success path and would strip the run-shape data (aec1) from the\nsuccess spend row.\n\n**Scope & safety.** Single call site for `record_call_spend` (the run() chokepoint — its\ndocstring notes it is \"the one chokepoint shared by both the external tier and the live\nprompt-eval\"), so no construct siblings. No parity siblings (the fake/override runners burn no\ntokens). Caller-dependency sweep: nothing depends on the ABSENCE of a spend row on the finalize\npath — only the c465 characterization test pinned the gap, updated here per AC. Restoration not\ncreation; no new dependency; the touched test is strengthened (gap → fix), not weakened.\n\n**Test (RED→GREEN, held-out, teeth).** `tests/unit/test_pydantic_ai_runner.py::\ntest_a_raise_in_finalize_outcome_still_logs_and_records_the_spend_row` (renamed from the\ncharacterization test per AC). Seen RED first (`0 == 1`), GREEN after fix; mutation check\n(re-introducing the unguarded ordering, run under an OS sandbox) returns it to RED. Full runner\nsuite (33) + lint + typecheck green."},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1788064621122584530,"uuid":"ceb5edd1-69c3-44b3-92e6-b77fc79ede9f"}